    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27c01036_45354624",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fpc1025.c",
        "patchSetId": 41
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1529242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-30T18:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t appear to be using the `rx_bufs` side so why not make the third parameters NULL?\n\nAs a side note, is it safe to use `trx` for both `tx_bufs` and `rx_bufs`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "726c1c594b2240889e8ba591c7e7a03f37357ed2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47bfb8f2_7245a73f",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/fingerprint/fpc1025.c",
        "patchSetId": 41
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T17:24:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We don\u0027t appear to be using the rx_bufs side\n\nWe do. `id` contains 0x0000, and after `spi_transceive_dt()` it contains 2 byte HWID in big endian, and `cmd` is 0x00, because the first byte we receive is 0x00.\n\n\n\u003e As a side note, is it safe to use trx for both tx_bufs and rx_bufs\n\nYes. SPI driver first loads the byte, performs the transfer and saves received byte. I can even find examples in Zephyr code https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/5174e94c91c560de8961da3e81a4b001473daa6d/drivers/sdhc/sdhc_spi.c#L390, though I must admit that it\u0027s not a common pattern.\n\nIf you feel like this can cause problems in future, I can split it into two buffers, it costs only one extra byte (to save first byte). This has also advantage that we don\u0027t send `id` contents, so we can prevent from accidental leak if somebody forgets to initialize `id` variable.",
      "parentUuid": "27c01036_45354624",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "726c1c594b2240889e8ba591c7e7a03f37357ed2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
