      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T17:24:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I refer here to [the original PAL implementation](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/driver/fingerprint/fpc/bep/fpc_sensor_spi.c;l\u003d35-38;drc\u003df108d67192739dd055089d397a771c484db91524). In the original implementation we always flush SPI (release in Zephyr world) if the size is equal to real image size. We also have `leave_cs_asserted` which says if we should keep CS asserted.\n\nI don\u0027t know why the original implementation checks the size, so I added code that prints warning if there is a conflict between these. Unfortunately, the warning never appeared.\n\n@tomhughes@chromium.org maybe you know why the original PAL implementation checks the size?",
